==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Zangief Cat CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Zangief Cat CC, is surprisingly competent for an Anti-[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] midrange nuker, and can be compared to [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] in more ways than one. He has higher base stats and a lower cost compared to Pizza, along with [[Immune to Slow|Slow Immunity]] and most important of all, [[Savage Blow]].

At Lv.30 his damage is nothing to sneeze at, being able to deal up to ''240,000 damage'' (388,000 at Lv.50) in a single Savage Blow. This makes him a phenomenal counter to most [[Teacher Bun Bun]] variants, as well as high HP tanks like [[The Face]] and [[Cli-One]]. Though it should be noted that he faces steep competition from [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], who is far faster, cheaper, and more spammable. Zangief Cat CC's advantages are mainly in his Area Attacks, and higher range.

It is also worth keeping in mind that Zangief Cat CC can't reposition as easily as Pizza, and he has a longer attack rate, along with a longer recharge time when compared to Pizza Cat. This isn't even mentioning the fact that Pizza Cat gets access to many great [[Talents]].

Despite his flaws, he's a must get unit!

